  "note": "Overall recall 0.7308 -> 0.8205, unseen 0.5532 -> 0.7021, high+medium 0.7544, visible 0.7436. `local` is the opt-out, not the default, from this wave on; it moves less than `ip` on purpose, because MLV101/MLV102/MLV103's new paths are ip-only by construction (3.11 R1.5). Recall wave, 2026-09-15 (branch `consolidate`), the whole Track-3 change set, measured against the figures this file carried at main b46a27c. What earned it: (R1) `--dataflow ip` became the product default from the one constant `ir.build_ir.DEFAULT_DATAFLOW` (CONTRACTS 3.11 R1.1-R1.5), `local` stays a shipped, gated opt-out. (R2) two new knowledge tables - `knowledge/pandas_tbl.py` (pandas beyond the shape-preserving hop) and `knowledge/stats_tbl.py` (statsmodels, Prophet, HuggingFace `evaluate`, torchmetrics) - plus the rest of the Keras Model surface and pandas indexer stripping (14.2 F16-F21). Nine new roles, none keyed on by any rule. (R3) `core/workspace_ops.py` draws the three call shapes through workspace-defined objects - constructing a workspace class, invoking one, and a factory's returned object - with `ReturnSlot.opaque` for a factory nobody can follow, and object carriage through dict/tuple literals, dataclass fields, `self.<attr>` and rebinding wrappers (5.3 A7-A12'). (R4) `rules/valuetype.py` types LOGITS/PROBS/PREDS through a workspace helper's `return` and a `.detach().cpu().numpy()` tail for MLV305/306/401/402, which pay one IP_HOP_WEIGHT for the crossing (5.3 A13, 14.2 R19-R21). (R5) interprocedural detection paths for MLV101 (through a return), MLV102 (through a CV fold index) and MLV103 (through a callee), the split-dictionary spelling for MLV111, and two corrections to MLV205's accumulator test (14.2 R13-R18). Graph fidelity 127/139 = 0.9137 -> 163/164 = 0.9939: the denominator moved because hf_no_eval and lightning_manual were hand-labelled with `graph` blocks in the same wave, each recording its provenance in `graph.drawnBy`; scored against the old denominator alone it is 138/139. PRECISION IS UNCHANGED AND IS THE CONSTRAINT: 1.0 with 0 forbidden and 0 unlabelled findings in BOTH dataflow modes, 0 findings on `analyzer/tests/clean` and on `samples/vision_pipeline_clean` in both modes. Recall may only ratchet up; a forbidden finding is never tolerated. Regenerate with `python tools/accuracy.py --update-baseline` and say in the commit body which change earned the new number.",
